Ancient Greek: first reading and scholarly preparation (@greek-language-sources: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @greek-sources, #contains @greek-source-ancient-greek) { r_1XJQDKNZ29XC8S5CD8GS4YK3EH
For closer reading of the arguments and more informed comparisons between translations, learn Ancient Greek. Begin with [Philip S. Peek's Ancient Greek I](../sources/Ancient-Greek-Peek.lingua#r_1D87YRHMAM7FHZH3VCDY9JTHGX) and the [optional reading practice](Read-original-texts.lingua#r_1Q07KPDNG2JTY7HRWQY5H6T5MJ).

The first dialogues and foundation survey can be studied through English and Portuguese readings. Language study can begin alongside them. The later [Greek dossier](../research/Philological-study.lingua#r_353E4E4WH3BWFHHJNZMPKBPEXF) requires working command of the passages used for scholarly research and full completion.

